.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
pwd
- print the working directory
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
pwd
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Pwd writes the full path name of the current directory.
.sp
There is no system call that answers the question, so pwd walks
upward: it reads the current directory, finds the entry for "..",
stats it to learn which inode the parent is, then reads the parent to
find the name the child is filed under, and repeats until it reaches
the root.  The names it collects on the way up are printed in reverse.
.sp
Pwd takes no arguments.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
NOTES
.in +5
.br
The one that came with micronix did not work.  This is a rewrite.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
